{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\( z_{2002} \\) given the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z+i}{z-i} \\) and the sequence defined by \\( z_n = F(z_{n-1}) \\) with \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\), we need to investigate the behavior of the sequence.\n\nFirst, let's compute the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns.\n\n1. **Compute \\( z_1 \\):**\n   \\[\n   z_1 = F(z_0) = F\\left( \\frac{1}{137} + i \\right) = \\frac{\\left( \\frac{1}{137} + i \\right) + i}{\\left( \\frac{1}{137} + i \\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i\n   \\]\n\n2. **Compute \\( z_2 \\):**\n   \\[\n   z_2 = F(z_1) = F(1 + 274i) = \\frac{(1 + 274i) + i}{(1 + 274i) - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i}\n   \\]\n   To simplify \\( \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\), we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i - 275 \\cdot 273i^2}{1 - (273i)^2} = \\frac{1 + 2i + 275 \\cdot 273}{1 + 273^2} = \\frac{1 + 2i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263 + i}{37265}\n   \\]\n   This is a complex number, but it's not immediately clear if there's a simpler form. Instead, let's check if \\( F(z) \\) has a periodic behavior.\n\n","prefix_end":1199,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,1147,15159,17,15,15,17,92,1124,8,2661,279,729,17767,434,13174,8,284,1124,37018,90,89,21212,15170,89,17600,92,1124,8,323,279,8500,4512,553,17767,1147,1089,284,434,13174,15159,77,12,16,5410,1124,8,448,17767,1147,62,15,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,16,18,22,92,488,600,1124,701,582,1184,311,19314,279,7709,315,279,8500,382,5338,11,1077,594,12564,279,1156,2421,3793,315,279,8500,311,10542,894,12624,382,16,13,3070,46254,17767,1147,62,16,1124,1648,1019,256,1124,9640,256,1147,62,16,284,434,13174,62,15,8,284,43